 and internationally. It operates through Etsy and Depop segments. The company operates Etsy marketplace that connects artisans with various consumers; and Depop, a fashion resale marketplace. It also provides marketplace activities, including transaction offsite advertising, payments processing, and listing fees, as well as from optional seller services, which include on-site advertising and shipping labels. The company was formerly known as Indieco, Inc changed its name to Etsy, Inc. in June 2006. Etsy, Inc. was founded in 2005 and is headquartered in Brooklyn, New York.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Kruti  Patel Goyal | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 27%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $285K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $103K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Etsy, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $7.7B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +27% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 47% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 38-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 70% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $678M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage of 14\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 10.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 54% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5447991761071063},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Chewy vs. Etsy: Which Consumer Stock Is a Better Buy for 2027?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/chewy-vs-etsy-consumer-stock-123402000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794487151.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Has Etsy (NYSE:ETSY) Turned the Corner as Shopper Numbers Grow?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/has-etsy-nyseetsy-turned-the-corner-as-shopper-numbers-grow","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794481560.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Has Etsy (NYSE:ETSY) Finally Turned the Corner?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/has-etsy-nyseetsy-finally-turned-the-corner","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794462000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Etsy (NASDAQ:ETSY) Build On Its Stronger Quarter?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/can-etsy-nasdaqetsy-build-on-its-stronger-quarter","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794200700.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.677,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Etsy Doubters Got Wrong","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-etsy/etsy/news/what-etsy-doubters-got-wrong","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794104472.077,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Etsy (NYSE:ETSY) Stock: Insider Charles Baker Sells 1,407 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com