e 27 covering analysts target $98.48 on average, 11% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 47% clears the cost of capital of 8.8% by 38pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.22).","It runs a 70% gross margin and converts 24% of revenue into free cash flow, or 15% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 4.25x.","It spends 15.6% of revenue on R&D and 8.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.7x net debt to EBITDA ($1.6B of cash against $3.0B of debt), with interest covered 14.4x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.57 in the distress zone."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.0% over 3 years, 10.8% over 5 years and 26.6% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 30%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 0.0% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 41%.","Capex runs only 0.2x depreciation (0.5% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 26, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.4%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (16 sales, net $5.7M sold).","It returns 10.1% a year to shareholders (10.1% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 7.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 16.1% of the float, 3.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 2,375 employees, each generates about $1.2M of revenue, 3.2x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 26.6% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $285K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.2M (2x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $103K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":58,"head":"Watch: composite 44, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $73.63.","pros":["Composite 44, above the 39 line (gates 11/25)","ROIC 46.7% vs WACC 8.8%","FCF margin 23.5%","Revenue grew 10.8%/yr over 5y","P/FCF 11.3x vs sector 16.7x"],"cons":["Trades 3% above fair value of $86.62","Net debt/EBITDA 3.7x","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.57)","P/E 23.7x vs sector 18.8x","EV/EBITDA 16.5x vs sector 10.7x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":73.63,"vc":{"base":86.62,"base_src":"dcf","bear":53.39,"bull":139.52,"alt_median":14.64,"n_alt":1,"gap":6.3682,"dispersion":0.761,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (76% dispersion)","DCF is 637% above the other models' median ($14.64)"]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[34.41,47.04,53.39,58.94,63.51,68.33,72.33,76.33,79.55,83.24,87.55,91.79,95.66,100.21,105.58,112.89,119.25,127.32,139.52,158.93,201.9],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.789,"discount_rate":0.177,"terminal_growth":0.015,"exit_multiple":0.019},"ticker":"ETSY","date":"2026-11-13"}